## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design ingestion-time data quality with multi-tenant constraints and governance, including quarantine handling, catalog evolution, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Ingestion-time validation
- Per-tenant schema drift handling
- Quarantine DLQ and audit trails
- Glue catalog evolution and Athena access
- OpenTelemetry tracing and SLA alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo validator sketch
exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const record = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(evt.data, 'base64').toString());
  const valid = record.tenant_id && typeof record.tenant_id === 'string' && record.fields;
  if (!valid) throw new Error('Invalid');
  return { validity: 'ok' };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale the validator for 1M events/sec?
- How would you model per-tenant schema drift and auto-remediation?

## Why This Is Asked
A practical, end-to-end data validation and routing exercise that stays beginner-friendly while testing data quality, deduping, and observability.

## Key Concepts
- Kinesis Data Streams and Lambda triggers
- JSON validation, numeric ranges, and per-record scoring
- Severity-based routing to S3 Parquet
- DynamoDB for deduplication (deviceId+ts)
- DLQ handling and CloudWatch alerts
- LocalStack test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const rec = JSON.parse(Buffer.from(event.Records[0].kinesis.data, 'base64').toString());
  if (!rec.deviceId || !rec.ts) throw new Error('Missing fields');
  if (typeof rec.temp !== 'number' || typeof rec.humidity !== 'number') throw new Error('Bad types');
  let sev = 0;
  if (rec.temp > 80 || rec.humidity > 90) sev = 2; else sev = 0;
  // placeholder: write to DynamoDB for dedupe, route to S3 parquet in two prefixes by severity
  return { status: 'ok', severity: sev };
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test idempotency and dedupe in DynamoDB?
- How would you simulate and monitor lag and DLQ depth in CloudWatch during a spike?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests observability discipline across streaming steps, understanding of tracing propagation, and cost-aware monitoring in a multi-region DVA pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry integration in Lambda
- Trace propagation across services (trace-id, span)
- CloudWatch metrics, CloudWatch Logs, and X-Ray integration
- Kinesis streaming observability and SLA alerting
- Trade-offs: sampling rate, ADOT deployment, and cost implications

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry setup for a Lambda
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { getNodeAutoInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrumentations-node');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-trace-otlp-grpc');
const sdk = new NodeSDK({
  instrumentations: [getNodeAutoInstrumentation()],
  traceExporter: new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: 'http://ADOT-collector:4317' }),
